ce in my party. And sometimes, we've been in the majority.\par \par \uc2 RAHM EMANUEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Let's just hug it out then.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) What, what, what matters is, do you stand up for your principles, or don't you?\par \par \uc2 RAHM EMANUEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And, and there are lots of Republicans who will continue to stand against...\par \par \uc2 RAHM EMANUEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And you and the party is aimless when it comes to principles.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...will continue to stand against anti-Semitism and white supremacy and...\par \par \uc2 RAHM EMANUEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Hasn't.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yes, they have. There have been plenty Republicans who have.\par \par \uc2 YVETTE SIMPSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) They have not.\par \par \uc2 RAHM EMANUEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) They have not - I'm going to...\par \par \uc2 ALICE STEWART (REPUBLICAN STRATEGIST/CNN)\par \par \uc2 Well, the good thing, one thing is for sure, one thing is for sure...\par \par \uc2 RAHM EMANUEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...wait, wait a second. I, I apologize. I'm not going to take a lecture on anti-Semitism from Chris. And I love Chris, but I'm not going to do that.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Well...\par \par \uc2 RAHM EMANUEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Chris, you have a Republican member of the House of Representatives from Illinois, her and her husband, he's a state rep, who talked about Nazi ideology and legitimacy. You had people on the south, on the lawn of a House of Representatives who said six million is not enough, Camp Auschwitz, and did not drum to the condemnation of the Republican Party, because they are still of the view that the - Antifa and others were part of that protest. I am sorry. The party needs to - reject anti-Semitism, racism and xenophobia if it's going to be a majority party anywhere in the country that respects human rights.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And - Rahm, the - the majority of this party does reject it, and I disagree with you.\par \par \uc2 RAHM EMANUEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) It doesn't.\par \par \uc2 YVETTE SIMPSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) They don't.\par \par \uc2 ALICE STEWART (REPUBLICAN STRATEGIST/CNN)\par \par \uc2 And - they certainly do, and, and I will be one to say so. But the, the key to party you say being divided, one this is for sure. The Republican Party is united in their full-throated effort to try and stop these Progressive policies that Joe Biden is full-throated pushing forward when he campaigned as being a moderate. He is very far to the left. And that's what Republican...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) No Republican votes for his package. That is pretty clear.\par \par \uc2 YVETTE SIMPSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) These are not progressive, far-left policies.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yvette, before we go, I do want to ask you about Andrew Cuomo. We saw those headlines this morning. A second person has come forward with sexual harassment allegations. Can he survive this?\par \par \uc2 YVETTE SIMPSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) No, he shouldn't. I mean, honestly, you know, when you think about someone who is in a position of power like this, and we know, we've been here before, we've had these conversations around this table, and you take advantage of your relationship with women in the - and I believe these women, I, I always stand with women, then you should not be in a position of authority. And honestly, with, you know, Andrew Cuomo has had a very, very bad couple weeks with the issue with COVID and the nursing home facility, and this is just another shoe to drop.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Rahm?\par \par \uc2 RAHM EMANUEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) To the core question, one is, women need to be heard by all of us, respected and have the capacity to step forward and be listened to.\par \par \uc2 YVETTE SIMPSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) All of us.\par \par \uc2 RAHM EMANUEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Second, it has to be a robust and transparent process, not one that he came up with.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) So, the Attorney General?\par \par \uc2 YVETTE SIMPSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Right.\par \par \uc2 RAHM EMANUEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And it, whatever it is and it has to have...\par \par \uc2 YVETTE SIMPSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And he doesn't get to pick his own judge.\par \par \uc2 RAHM EMANUEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Just hold on. It has to have legitimacy. And right now, what it is, is the process itself is being questioned, let alone what happened. And for - everybody involved, given that it's a governor, et cetera, this, it needs robust transparency and a process that has legitimacy, whatever it concludes, and people need to have space to say what they have, what they believe happened to them, and we have to respect that space.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Alice?\par \par \uc2 ALICE STEWART (REPUBLICAN STRATEGIST/CNN)\par \par \uc2 And I think the key that is right, this is certainly troubling, we're hearing from key Democrats. Jerry Nadler says this is very troubling. And we've had state senators, one calling him a monster and, and he must go. And the key thing is, as Rahm says, these women should be heard. We should listen to them, they should have the environment and the space to speak. Also, the notion of due process for the accused, but what we're seeing is, instead of isolated allegations potential for a, a pattern of behavior, which is very disturbing, and an aggressive investigation needs to ensue.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Thirty seconds.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Listen, I agree with what everyone said about people and the women in this instance having be heard. These are very serious things. But I also want to caution. You know, there were a lot of people who jumped to conclusions on Brett Kavanaugh and what happened there. And I think we need to hear from Governor Cuomo. We need to be able to hear from him. He needs to have an opportunity to say what happened with, from his perspective.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And he has denied the allegations.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Right, and he...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Independent investigation?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Okay. Thank you all very much.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Coming up, more on the murder of Jamal Khashoggi, and exclusive interview with his friend and colleague from "The Washington Post," editorial page editor Fred Hiatt. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020210305eh2s00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SENATOR MAZIE HIRONO BIDEN LOOKS TO RECALIBRATE US SAUDI RELATIONS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,271 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 February 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2021 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, BILL, TRUMP, CPAC, GOP, SAUDI, PRINCE, IRAN\par \par \uc2 HIRONO, BIDEN, SAUDI, BILL, CUOMO, HATE CRIMES\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Let's bring in now Democratic Senator Mazie Hirono of Hawaii, a member of the \uc2 Senate Armed Services Committee\uc2 . Senator Hirono, thanks for joining us this morning. I do want to begin with that action against Saudi Arabia. President Biden said his team as I said, is going to be announcing more actions tomorrow. Should he be doing more to target the crown prince personally?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR MAZIE HIRONO (DEM-HAWAII) (\uc2 SENATE ARMED SERVICES COMMITTEE\uc2  MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 He is reassessing our relationship with Saudi Arabia, which is an ally. And I don't think the chapter is closed on the outcome of a disclosure of this report. That's my hope.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) So, what, what would you like to see done?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN LOOKS TO RECALIBRATE US SAUDI RELATIONS\par \par \uc2 SENATOR MAZIE HIRONO (DEM-HAWAII) (\uc2 SENATE ARMED SERVICES COMMITTEE\uc2  MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 I don't know because, you know - let's face it, George, it's a very complicated situation. Saudi Arabia is an ally, and, and so, yes, there are calls to, to do more. And I await the, the reassessment that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is going to engage in regarding Saudi Arabia, and the pause in arms - the arms sales, that, that I think hits Saudi Arabia, and I think that there will be more. I hope so.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Let's, let's talk about the COVID relief bill. The minimum wage, as we talked about, has been stripped from the Senate package, and there are a variety of proposals to respond to that. Senator Sanders is proposing to strip tax breaks to big companies who don't pay $15 an hour. Joe Manchin, on the other hand, and some Republicans are proposing a smaller increase. What's the best way to address this right now?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMS SCRAMBLE TO SAVE MINIMUM WAGE INCREASE\par \par \uc2 SENATOR MAZIE HIRONO (DEM-HAWAII) (\uc2 SENATE ARMED SERVICES COMMITTEE\uc2  MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 First of all, we need to get the massive COVID bill passed, and we know that we're going to have to do it without any Republican support. And the question should be, you know, it's on Republicans why we're having a hard time with, with getting the COVID bill done bipartisan way in the Congress, not across the country. So, we are looking for other ways to, in effect, require increase in the minimum wage, which hasn't been increased in over 10 years or so.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) But can the bill be passed if some minimum wage increase is included in the COVID relief package, or should it be separate?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR MAZIE HIRONO (DEM-HAWAII) (\uc2 SENATE ARMED SERVICES COMMITTEE\uc2  MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 According to the parliamentarian, it would not be, we can't do it. We can't raise the, the minimum wage directly, so we're going to look for indirect ways to effect that.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And that, that would be restricting the tax breaks for corporations who don't pay?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR MAZIE HIRONO (DEM-HAWAII) (\uc2 SENATE ARMED SERVICES COMMITTEE\uc2  MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 Yes, among other, in other ways.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And you, you support that?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR MAZIE HIRONO (DEM-HAWAII) (\uc2 SENATE ARMED SERVICES COMMITTEE\uc2  MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 Yes, I do. I will support all, all kind of ways. I mean, I, I basically support raising the minimum wage in the COVID bill, because that is a huge part of economic recovery. The people who are suffering most from the minimum wage and what's happening in the, in the pandemic are the essential workers. Many of them are women. Many of them are getting paid very low wages. $7.25 an hour is $15,000 a year. That's poverty level.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE \uc2 NEW YORK TIMES\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Let me ask you about Governor \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  of New York. "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " is reporting this morning that a second state employee has come forward accusing him of sexual harassment. We see "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 ," right there. He denies the charges. You've been outspoken about sexual harassment charges in the past, said men should shut up and step up during the \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  hearings. You've asked every nominee about sexual harassment during confirmation hearings.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR MAZIE HIRONO (DEM-HAWAII) (\uc2 SENATE ARMED SERVICES COMMITTEE\uc2  MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 Mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CUOMO FACES SECOND SEXUAL HARASSMENT ALLEGATION\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) What's the proper response to these allegations against Governor Cuomo?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING CALLS FOR INDEPENDENT CUOMO INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 SENATOR MAZIE HIRONO (DEM-HAWAII) (\uc2 SENATE ARMED SERVICES COMMITTEE\uc2  MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 Well, the proper response for any of these kinds of allegations of reprehensible, inexcusable behavior is to listen to the mainly women who come forward, because it takes great courage for them to come forward, to listen to them, and then to do the appropriate investigation and corroboration of the allegations. In the case of Governor Cuomo, it seems to me that the New York attorney general would be the independent entity to conduct such an investigation.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yeah. Not, not the investigation that he's announced himself?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR MAZIE HIRONO (DEM-HAWAII) (\uc2 SENATE ARMED SERVICES COMMITTEE\uc2  MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 No. I wouldn't consider that to be - independent. It should be, I would say the Attorney General of New York.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Finally, Senator, you were the first Asian American woman elected to the Senate. And this past year, we've seen a striking surge in anti-Asian hate crimes here in america. Why is this happening, and what should be done about it?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALARMING RISE IN ANTI-ASIAN HATE CRIMES\par \par \uc2 SENATOR MAZIE HIRONO (DEM-HAWAII) (\uc2 SENATE ARMED SERVICES COMMITTEE\uc2  MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 It's happening because we didn't have leadership at the top, starting from President Trump calling it the China virus and the kung flu and, and all of that, which, apparently, it unleashed this kind of targeted hate crimes against Asian Americans. It's, and the increase is dramatic. And in fact, just last week in New York, a person who was just walking down the street gets, got knifed. He is in serious condition.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR MAZIE HIRONO (DEM-HAWAII) (\uc2 SENATE ARMED SERVICES COMMITTEE\uc2  MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 And soon thereafter, four people walking in New York were knifed, one died. In California, you have incidents of 90-year-old people being knocked down, attacked, one, that person died. And so, I'm glad that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , unlike Trump has put the, the, this issue forward through his - executive memorandum, which by the way, contains many of the provisions that I had put in a resolution that I tried to pass last year condemning targeted hate crimes against Asian Americans.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR MAZIE HIRONO (DEM-HAWAII) (\uc2 SENATE ARMED SERVICES COMMITTEE\uc2  MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 And the, the idea is for the Attorney General, our new attorney, soon-to-be new attorney general, to work with state county officials and community groups to prevent and prosecute these kind of hate crimes. So, it's being recognized by President Biden, and that's, you know, leadership throughout our country should condemn, in no uncertain terms. When you have Asian-Americans afraid to walk down the street for the fear of being knifed, this is an issue that needs to be dealt with.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Senator Hirono, thanks for your time this morning.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR MAZIE HIRONO (DEM-HAWAII) (\uc2 SENATE ARMED SERVICES COMMITTEE\uc2  MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 Thank you. Aloha.\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020210305eh2s00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FIRST 100 DAYS HOUSE PASSES BIDEN'S $1.9T COVID RELIEF BILL\b0\par\par\uc2 1,180 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 February 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2021 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, BILL, TRUMP, CPAC, GOP, SAUDI, PRINCE, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) We're going to cover it all this morning starting with my "This Week" co-anchors Martha Raddatz and \uc2 Jon Karl\uc2 . And Jon, let me begin with you right now. That vote in House on the President's COVID relief package, about as close as it could get. There's no votes to spare in the Senate, where the Democrats are now wrestling with how to handle that stripping of the $15 minimum wage from the bill.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST 100 DAYS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE PASSES BIDEN'S $1.9T COVID RELIEF BILL\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Good morning, George. Biden is on the verge of his first major legislative victory. And make no mistake, this would be a really big one. But there is absolutely no room for error. The COVID relief bill passed in the House, as you mentioned, without a single Republican vote. There are almost certainly no Republican votes in the Senate, either, and that means he can't afford to lose a single Democrat. Thanks to the ruling by the Senate parliamentarian, the provision raising the minimum wage to $15 an hour is not in the bill. But, with two Democrats opposed to it, the $15 minimum wage doesn't appear to have 50 votes, regardless.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE PASSES COVID BILL WITHOUT ANY GOP SUPPORT\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Some progressives are pushing for an all-out war to save the minimum wage increase, even if that means calling for the parliamentarian to be fired. But here's the bottom line from the Biden White House, even without the minimum wage, this $1.9 trillion bill has almost everything that Biden wants. They will take it. They will consider it a huge victory, even if that means the hike in the minimum wage is gone for now and it's a battle to fight another time.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATE PARLIAMENTARIAN RULES AGAINST MINIMUM WAGE HIKE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Meantime, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is coming back. His presidency was far from normal. His post-presidency seems headed in the same direction, extraordinary that he's giving this speech just weeks after the, after leaving office. And it's, he's still, it's going to be clear from what we've seen in the speeches at CPAC already, that he's still got an iron grip on the GOP.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP RETURNS TO SPOTLIGHT WITH CPAC SPEECH\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Oh - no, no doubt about that, George. Back in 2016, Trump actually skipped CPAC because there was talk that conservative activists could walk out on his speech. They didn't consider him a real Conservative. Now, they're calling it, some people, TPAC, the Trump Political Action Conference. And speaker after speaker has declared that Trump is the dominant force or the leader of the Republican Party.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Any Republicans who have been seen to defy Trump have been banished. There is no \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  at CPAC, no \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , no Nikki Haley, not even \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 . And even, by the way, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , who said that Trump was responsible for the riot on January 6th, who said that Trump could be prosecuted, even suggested that he should be, he said this week that he would support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  if he is the Republican nominee in 2024.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MCCONNELL: 'ABSOLUTELY' WOULD SUPPORT TRUMP IN 2024\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) I've spoken over the past couple of days with several people who have been talking to Trump. He is plotting his reemergence. He is still falsely claiming the election was stolen from him, often going on and on and on in these conversations about the individual states, and he's talking about getting revenge on Republicans who have defied him. I suspect that is essentially the message that you'll hear from him today.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And we will listening today. And, of course, he's also facing possible prosecution in New York and Georgia. Let me bring in Martha Raddatz, our chief global affairs anchor, as well. And let's start with President Biden and Saudi Arabia, Martha. He declassified that intelligence, spoke with the King of Saudi Arabia, not with the crown prince. But he's facing real blowback for not doing more to punish the crown prince for his approval of that killing.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) It, it's really hard to see, George, what any, any sort of punishment the crown prince got other than that public rebuke. No visa restrictions, no sanctions. Listen to what candidate \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said. "Khashoggi was, in fact, murdered and dismembered, and I believe on the order of the crown prince, and I would make it very clear we were not going to sell more weapons to them. We were going to make them pay the price and make them the pariah that they are."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN DECLINES TO PENALIZE SAUDI CROWN PRINCE\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) As far as weapons even go, there's a pause in weapons. They may not sell them defense, offensive weapons, only defensive weapons, but it's very unclear what that would be. Adam Schiff is saying, look, the crown prince has blood on his hands. You punished the people who carried out the order, but have not punished the person who ordered the killing, George. So, there's a lot of blowback to this. And yet, and you have to wonder if there's another Saudi dissident who does not live in America, who does not work for an American newspaper, what the world will think and what the crown prince will think.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: US ANNOUNCES NEW SANCTIONS TO PROTECT DISSIDENTS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And we'll be watching to see. The President says there will be more coming tomorrow on Saudi Arabia. Meantime, we also saw his first military action this week, striking at Iranian-backed militias, even as his team is working to engage with Iran on their nuclear program.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: US LAUNCHES AIRSTRIKE TARGETING IRANIAN-BACKED MILITIAS\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And, and that's exactly what's happening, George. As you know well, it's, it's a little easier to campaign than govern. They did carry out this airstrike in Syria to a - compound of Iranian-backed militias, but it was the least lethal option. But \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had to act. There was a rocket attack on a coalition base in Iraq, and there were contractors wounded. There was one contractor who was working for the Americans who was killed. A servicemember was also wounded. So, we had to fire back in some way, but he wants to get back to the negotiating table. The nuclear policy is a much bigger issue to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the administration.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Martha Raddatz, \uc2 Jon Karl\uc2 , thanks very much.\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020210305eh2s00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOUSE TO VOTE ON COVID RELIEF BILL DEMS FACE MAJOR SETBACK ON $15 MINIMUM WAGE\b0\par\par\uc2 556 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 February 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST STRIKE\par \par \uc2 AIRSTRIKES, BIDEN, SYRIA, IRAN, MILITIA, AUSTIN\par \par \uc2 COVID-10, VACCINE, FDA, EUA, DOSES, \uc2 JOHNSON & JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, COVID, STIMULUS, MINIMUM WAGE, CAPITOL\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Okay, Steve, thanks. We're gonna go back to Washington now and the House getting ready to pass President Biden's nearly $2 trillion COVID relief bill, but the attempt to include a new $15 minimum wage suffered a setback overnight. Congressional correspondent Rachel Scott has the latest on where things stand. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE TO VOTE ON COVID RELIEF BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMS FACE MAJOR SETBACK ON $15 MINIMUM WAGE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) George, good morning. And the headline here is that $15 an hour minimum wage increase will likely not be included in the final version of this COVID relief package. The House is still on track to pass a version of this bill today, but overnight in the Senate, a setback. Democrats have laid the groundwork to be able to pass this bill on their own without any Republican support, but that does come with limitations. And so in the Senate you had this policy ruling saying that that $15 an hour minimum wage increase cannot be included in their version of the bill.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) The White House says President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is disappointed by this. He is urging Congress to act and pass this bill quickly. It will likely make it easier for the Senate to pass this bill. You had two moderate Senate Democrats who were opposed to that minimum wage increase. But lawmakers here are up against a deadline. On March 14th unemployment benefits for millions of Americans expire. They want to get this bill on President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's desk before then. So this would extend those unemployment benefits. It would also include $1400 in stimulus checks to most Americans. $350 billion in aid to state and local government, plus billions more for vaccine distribution, COVID testing and grants for schools. Now, Republicans still opposed to that $1.9 trillion price tag, George, they want more targeted relief.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAPITOL SECURITY WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE CHIEF: MEMBERS OF MILITIA GROUPS "WANT TO BLOW UP THE CAPITOL"\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And, Rachel, we're also hearing now from the acting police chief up on Capitol Hill concerned with a really stark warning about another possible attack on the Capitol. Let's look.\par \par \uc2 YOGANANDA PITTMAN (ACTING POLICE CHIEF CAPITOL HILL)\par \par \uc2 We know that members of the militia groups that were present on January 6th have stated their desires that they want to blow up the Capitol and kill as many members as possible with a direct nexus to the State of the Union.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Now, that isn't even scheduled yet, that address to a joint session of Congress, but they are taking nothing for granted.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yeah, and this is really prompting new concerns, George, about security, so the acting police chief saying that while the fencing that you see around the United States Capitol is temporary, she believes the heightened security is absolutely necessary, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Rachel Scott, thanks very much. Cecilia.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020210310eh2q00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 COVID RELIEF BILL $1.9 TRILLION BILL WORKING WAY THROUGH CONGRESS\b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 February 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 COVID-19, WALENSKY, VACCINE, SUPER BOWL, BIDEN, CRANE\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, VARIANTS, ENGLAND, VIRUS MUTATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRACKING THE VARIANTS\par \par \uc2 IMPEACHMENT, TRIAL, TRUMP, RYAN, INSURRECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP IMPEACHMENT TRIAL\par \par \uc2 RELIEF BILL, BIDEN, TAX CREDIT, MINIMUM WAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVID RELIEF BILL\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Meantime, President Biden's nearly $2 trillion relief plan tonight working its way through Congress. And this evening, there is news, word of a proposal to send up to $3,600 per child to American families. There's also news tonight on efforts to raise the federal minimum wage to $15. Let's get right to our chief White House correspondent, Cecilia Vega, live at the White House tonight with late details for us. Cecilia?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: $1.9 TRILLION BILL WORKING WAY THROUGH CONGRESS\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Hey, David, good evening to you. On that tax credit, Democrats feel confident that this will ultimately end up in that nearly $2 trillion COVID relief package by the President. But let me show you what it does. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMOCRAT CHILD TAX CREDIT PROPOSAL\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It would be split into monthly payments, starting in July, $3,600 per child under the age of 6, $3,000 for kids 6 to 17 years old. That amount decreases for families earning more than $75,000 a year.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) The White House said today that President Biden is on board with this. But on that minimum wage, the $15 an hour minimum wage, they are hitting a major roadblock there, David. Take a look at this.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROPOSED $15 MINIMUM WAGE\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A nonpartisan study out today found that while it would give a major boost to low-income workers, it would also cost about 1.4 million jobs and add $54 billion to the deficit over the next decade. The White House is pushing back on those findings, but even President Biden is conceding now that this could be a loss, at this point. He says Democrats are gonna have to work their way up in separate legislation to that $15 an hour, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) All right, tracking this COVID relief plan. Cecilia Vega, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020210210eh280000e\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 GETTING THE JOB IN 2021 CHALLENGES OF FINDING WORK DURING THE PANDEMIC\b0\par\par\uc2 1,690 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 February 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACE AGAINST TIME\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, VACCINES, VARIANTS, GOUNDER, ZIENTS, DOSES\par \par \uc2 FAUCI, COVID-19, VACCINES, VARIANTS, SUPER BOWL\par \par \uc2 NOR'EASTER, BLIZZARD, SNOW, WINDS, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2 , RAID, SCHWARTZENBERGER, ALFIN, PIRO\par \par \uc2 BEZOS, CEO, AMAZON, SHAKE-UP, JASSY\par \par \uc2 IMPEACHMENT, TRUMP, HOUSE, DEFENSE, REPUBLICANS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, RESPECTS, SICKNICK, CAPITOL, RIOTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLAR EXPRESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2 , HENRY, CONCUSSIONS, RACE, LAWSUIT, ROBERTS\par \par \uc2 DIMEO, TRANSPLANT, FACE, HANDS, RODRIGUEZ\par \par \uc2 JULIA, \uc2 GOOGLE\uc2 , SONG\par \par \uc2 VACCINATIONS, DISTRIBUTION, VARIANTS\par \par \uc2 STORM, NOR'EASTER\par \par \uc2 NAACP\uc2  IMAGE AWARDS, CHU, "WICKED", DOLPHIN, SUPER BOWL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NAACP\uc2  IMAGE AWARDS ANNOUNCE NOMINEES\par \par \uc2 FACE, TRANSPLANT, HAND, RODRIGUEZ, \uc2 NYU\uc2  LANGONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NYU LANGONE HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GOLDEN GLOBES, NOMINATIONS\par \par \uc2 EXERCISING, LIVING ROOM, WORKOUT\par \par \uc2 BAGEL, ADJEPONG, PHILLIPS\par \par \uc2 JOB, WOMEN, ZUCKER, BECKER, EATMON, WASSERMAN\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Back now with navigating the workforce during the pandemic. It can be a challenging time. We all know this. But women in the US, they're losing more than five million jobs. We caught up with three determined women looking for the secrets to resetting their job search, and the career coach helping ladies get paid.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) On the hunt for a job? You are not alone.\par \par \uc2 ALISHA ZUCKER (JOB SEEKER)\par \par \uc2 Hey, I'm Alisha. And I'm coming to you live from a place that I often do conference calls, my three old's toddler bed.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For mom, Alisha Zucker, searching for a job during the pandemic has had its share of challenges.\par \par \uc2 ALISHA ZUCKER (JOB SEEKER)\par \par \uc2 I really care about corporate culture. How do I figure this out during a remote interview.\par \par \uc2 KELLY BECKER (JOB SEEKER)\par \par \uc2 My pandemic job search, what a roller coaster.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Kelly Becker has her own questions on finding a job that's the best fit.\par \par \uc2 KELLY BECKER (JOB SEEKER)\par \par \uc2 I've been unemployed over 270 days. I've put in over 500 and some applications. How should I reset my job strategy?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And for Temaya Eatmon, there's a real sense of urgency to getting back into the workforce.\par \par \uc2 TEMAYA EATMON (JOB SEEKER)\par \par \uc2 I have a goal to find or land my dream job in the next 60 to 90 days, so any tips?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNEMPLOYMENT STATISTICS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The unemployment rate hitting an unprecedented 14.8 percent last April before declining to a still elevated 6.7 percent in December, with women losing 5.4 million jobs since the start of the pandemic, experiencing the majority of pandemic-related job losses.\par \par \uc2 CLAIRE WASSERMAN (FOUNDER & AUTHOR OF "LADIES GET PAID")\par \par \uc2 There are changes, serious changes with serious consequences that we need to address if all of us, and not just women, are going to succeed.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Claire Wasserman, author of the new book "Ladies Get Paid," has made it her mission to help women overcome barriers in the workforce. "GMA" matching Claire up with our viewers for one-on-one advice.\par \par \uc2 CLAIRE WASSERMAN (FOUNDER & AUTHOR OF "LADIES GET PAID")\par \par \uc2 This is a fantastic time to really dig into your values, your goals, your priorities.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And for job seekers, tapping into new strategies could be key to getting the job.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And Claire Wasserman joins us now. You were so cute. When I mentioned your book in the piece you went, yay, you started clapping for yourself. I know, it's so exciting when you see it on "GMA" like that, but it's a great book. And you're really helping a lot of people like the three women that we just profiled. It's different out there right now. So how can we all hit the reset button when it comes to a job search?\par \par \uc2 CLAIRE WASSERMAN (FOUNDER & AUTHOR OF "LADIES GET PAID")\par \par \uc2 Thank you for having me and, yes, I was going like this. Listen, this is a really hard time for women. And the first thing I want everybody to remember watching right now, you are not alone. Here's my silver lining, though. This is a great time to really reflect and possibly reset.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GET A JOB, RESET JOB SEARCH STRATEGY\par \par \uc2 CLAIRE WASSERMAN (FOUNDER & AUTHOR OF "LADIES GET PAID")\par \par \uc2 I wanna make sure that you are going in a direction, like I said, it has to be aligned with what you deeply want and sort of truly need in your life. But once you've done that, I want you to do an inventory of your online presence, right? How are you coming across? And this includes your resume, of course. But you need feedback. Feedback can be tough to get. So think about who are you going to ask to get a little bit of perspective.\par \par \uc2 CLAIRE WASSERMAN (FOUNDER & AUTHOR OF "LADIES GET PAID")\par \par \uc2 But hold on. Before you even submit your application, this can be really overwhelming, right? We saw that with Alisha. A lot of days that she's been unemployed, so let's get organized. Let's get organized. Let's set some goals. But break those goals down into mini goals. Otherwise you're not gonna reach them. And part of that is how are you gonna hold yourself accountable and, I think most importantly, how are you going to reward yourself, right? Again, this can be really, really tough.\par \par \uc2 CLAIRE WASSERMAN (FOUNDER & AUTHOR OF "LADIES GET PAID")\par \par \uc2 The last thing I wanted to mention about resetting your job strategy is, get some support. All right. Seventy-five to eighty percent of jobs are actually filled internally or through networking. So I would have you go ahead, reach out to people who work at the company so that they can advocate for you on the inside.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) That's all great advice. How about the virtual interview? It's so difficult for a lot of people. So what suggestions do you have to help with our skills virtually interviewing?\par \par \uc2 CLAIRE WASSERMAN (FOUNDER & AUTHOR OF "LADIES GET PAID")\par \par \uc2 Well, first, you wanna look good. I talked about this with Temaya. We've gotta get the lighting, the setup. You better believe I have all the light rings around me. Also, you only have this little box to work with so my question to you is, how are you going to convey your personality? I got my pink blazer. You see I took my time setting up the background, so that's the first step.\par \par \uc2 CLAIRE WASSERMAN (FOUNDER & AUTHOR OF "LADIES GET PAID")\par \par \uc2 Second step is, and I'm trying to do this right now, energy. Bring energy, right? Gesticulate, hands. If you need to do this before you get on, again, all the things that I just did. I want you to talk about your wins but not just sort of, you know, what you did but also how you did it. Use language that's in the job description. Use language that the company puts on their website about their company culture.\par \par \uc2 CLAIRE WASSERMAN (FOUNDER & AUTHOR OF "LADIES GET PAID")\par \par \uc2 But, like I said, you have to tie it to your impact. It's always, always about the bottom line. How have you made the company money? That could include how you saved the company money. We know that women are good multi-taskers, we're efficient. So you definitely wanna talk about that. It's also about how you did it because that's gonna show who you are. Your process, how you think, your potential. Tell that story. You know, because, again, they're hiring you to be part of a team. So what's the team dynamic going to look like with you? This is the time to talk about it.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Only have 15 seconds left. You know there are a lot of people that are getting discouraged. They've been out there for this. So how could we stay motivated?\par \par \uc2 CLAIRE WASSERMAN (FOUNDER & AUTHOR OF "LADIES GET PAID")\par \par \uc2 First, I think too oftentimes we see our jobs as a measure of our worth. So when we don't have one, it really hits our self-esteem. So please, use this time to take care of yourself. Also, if you're not getting the job you want, can you create the job that you want? Okay, this could be a time to start a side hustle or maybe support someone else's. This is gonna keep you motivated and also maybe give you something to talk about during the interview.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Oh, beautiful. Hey, Claire, congratulations on the book and thank you so much for offering your tips and advice. And I wanna let everybody know that you can find more tips from Claire on our website. And her book "Ladies Get Paid" is available, it's on the Jumbotron right now, Claire. Oh, you're on the Jumbotron with the book. Congratulations again. Oh, I love to see that when that happens. Let's get now with Ginger. Ginger.\par \par \uc2 CLAIRE WASSERMAN (FOUNDER & AUTHOR OF "LADIES GET PAID")\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) You're welcome.\par \par \uc2 GINGER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yes, Robin, I wanted to take a moment because Bruce is always envious of Riva. And so my dog Bruce just wanted to come and have his moment in the snow. Actually, he just wanted to come outside and play.\par \par \uc2 GINGER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But I wanted to share with you something I'd love to try some day. Look at this. It is a real life Mary Poppins on the ice in British Columbia. How cool would that be as long as the ice were fully formed, of course?\par \par \uc2 GINGER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Taking a look at the, oh, my goodness, they noticed that they could, they were starting to get pushed and so they grabbed an umbrella, and it worked. All right. That's the big picture. Bruce, come here, get your moment. Let's get a check a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020210211eh230000o\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORK FROM HOME FASHION LOOK PROFESSIONAL WHILE STAYING COMFORTABLE\b0\par\par\uc2 904 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 January 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CORONAVIRUS CRISIS\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, VACCINE, ROLLOUT, VARIANTS, WALENSKY\par \par \uc2 FAUCI, COVID-19, TRAVEL, VARIANTS, VACCINE, DEATH THREATS\par \par \uc2 IMPEACHMENT, TRUMP, INSURRECTION, KLOBUCHAR, SWALWELL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, EXECUTIVE ACTIONS, TRANSGENDER, COVID RELIEF\par \par \uc2 MEGA MILLIONS, WINNER, HARRIS, TICKET, JACKPOT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SUPER BOWL, BRADY, MAHOMES, BUCS, CHIEFS\par \par \uc2 KING, TRIBUTES, TALK SHOW, CAREER\par \par \uc2 MINERS, TRAPPED, TWO WEEKS, RESCUE, DEATHS\par \par \uc2 COVID 19, \uc2 MIAMI HEAT\uc2 , DOGS, JAFARIAN, OTTO\par \par \uc2 DENNIS, GYMNASTICS, MUSIC\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, VACCINES, TRAVEL BAN, FAUCI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CORONAVIRUS CRISIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VACCINE ROLLOUT RAMPS UP AMID GROWING VARIANT CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, IMPEACHMENT, TRIAL, SENATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP IMPEACHMENT SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "INCITEMENT OF INSURRECTION" ARTICLE BEING SENT TO SENATE TODAY\par \par \uc2 DIAMOND, BRAZIL, GIRL SCOUT COOKIES\par \par \uc2 SIWA, SEXUALITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 MENDES, SOCIAL MEDIAL, PARENTING, TECHNOLOGY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EVA MENDES STEPS BACK FROM SOCIAL MEDIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STAR SAYS DAUGHTER CALLS HER OUT OVER PHONE USE\par \par \uc2 SIMMONS, SOCIAL MEDIA, TECHNOLOGY, PARENTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUNG UP ON OUR PHONES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARNING SIGNS IT MAY BE IMPACTING OUR KIDS\par \par \uc2 CLOTHING, WORK\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Now to our series, "Make Work from Home Work for You."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORK FROM HOME FASHION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOOK PROFESSIONAL WHILE STAYING COMFORTABLE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) In the beginning of the pandemic, many people working remotely were sporting, okay, ultra-athleisure wear. But now, sweats might not always cut it. Becky Worley has some tips for making business and casual work together. Good morning, Becky.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Good morning, Robin. You are so right. We are in the marathon phase of work from home. So, now what does it mean look and feel professional remotely?\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Hey, everybody.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) What do you wear for Zoom calls? It initially centered on athleisure, sweatpants, leggings, hoodies. But there's a shift.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) We want comfy, but also professional. So, what do we call this look now? Zoom ready? Comfy chic? At-home profesh?\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We asked three professionals, who used to dress up, how they've adapted. First up, Arielle Parker (PH), she works in HR at a law firm. Pre-COVID...\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Oh, very business formal, which means, you know, blazers, shift dresses, (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Then the pandemic hit.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Comfort came first.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But now, her COVID 2.0 attire more professional.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I can invest in some really nice sweater pieces, and then sort of zhushing and diversifying it with earrings.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Arielle is employing what I call the mullet philosophy of Zoom fashion. It's business on top and maybe not party on the bottom, but certainly comfort. Leggings or joggers with a structured top and earrings. Boom. But for Patrice Kelly (PH), who works in finance, her evolution has been a bit more structured. Before COVID...\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I would a dress and, you know, heels or a skirt.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And while she went for comfort early on, she had an epiphany.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 You know, leggings and a sweater, and I was too comfortable to actually work and be productive. So, I went on and started wearing jeans every day on the bottom and just dressing up a little bit on the top.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And a useful accessory.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I won't have my headset and I just tuck it behind, so it's a little bit more fashionable.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, it's not just women. Mike Nicco is a meteorologist at affiliate KGO in San Francisco who's now doing his reports from home.\par \par \uc2 MIKE NICCO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The longer I stayed home, it got a little more casual, the tie was gone. We started to get bits of the sweaters and that's where you are now.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Don't forge the shorts and slippers.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Never forget the slippers. Okay, Becky, you have been working from home even before the pandemic. So, give us the dos and don'ts.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOS & DON'TS OF AT-HOME-STYLE\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Well, for one, video calls, Robin, are all about the silhouette you project.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VIDEO CALL FASHION DON'TS\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So, big ruffles or angular shoulders or lapels, that may not work in two dimensions. You also don't want an overly busy patterns, they can be distracting. And a sure winner, jewel tones.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VIDEO CALL FASHION DOS\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) You know, these emeralds, sapphires. They really are rich but they pop. And I want you to know, I always wear my leggings and my Uggs when I'm reporting just like I am now. Mullet style, business on the top, soft pants on the bottoms.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) So, you have Uggs on right now? You have that on? You're not gonna show us. There's proof in the pudding. Oh, nice. And nice extension, too. You stuck the landing. Thank you, Becky. Coming up, football great, that was really good. I will pull a hammy.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Peyton Manning gonna join us live. Exclusive sneak peek at his new Super Bowl commercial.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020210129eh1p0008z\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 EAT SMART MAKE WORK FROM HOME WORK FOR YOU\b0\par\par\uc2 810 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 January 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUNNING REPORT\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DOJ, LAWYER, PLOT,OVERTURN,ELECTION\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, EXECUTIVE, ORDERS, EMERGENCY, RELIEF\par \par \uc2 JANUARY, DEADLIEST, MONTH, VACCINE, SHORTAGES\par \par \uc2 VACCINE, ACCESS, PRESIDENT'S, PLAN\par \par \uc2 MAHOMES, CHIEFS, QUARTER BACK, CLEARED, AFC, CHAMPIONSHIP\par \par \uc2 MEGA, MILLIONS, WINNER, MICHIGAN\par \par \uc2 KIDS, COVID,CASES, RISING\par \par \uc2 COLORADO, COVID, PLAN, SCHOOLS\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, CHANGES, MASK, MANDATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN'S FIRST DAYS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, EXECUTIVE, ORDERS, EMERGENCY, RELIEF, PLANS\par \par \uc2 UK, VARIANT, DEADLIER, JANUARY, WORST, MONTH\par \par \uc2 INAUGURATION, INTERNET, BUZZIEST, MOMENTS\par \par \uc2 EAT, SMART, WORK, HOME, NUTRITION\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Well, time now to make work from home work for you. Registered dietitian and nutritionist Dawn Jackson Blatner has some tips to help us eat smart and make healthy choices all day long. Oh, I'm so glad you're here this morning. Thanks for being with us.\par \par \uc2 DAWN JACKSON-BLATNER (NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 Oh, thank you. Working from home, let's do it well.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) This is always the tricky part because you have all the access to the things at home, including the bad food. You have a trifecta you follow every morning to boost your energy and immunity. Tell us about it.\par \par \uc2 DAWN JACKSON-BLATNER (NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 Okay, here's the trifecta. First, water. You wake up the most dehydrated in the morning. So drink that water to energize you, boost your immunity. But also it puts a good dent in, you know, all the water you need to drink throughout the day so it gets you started on the right foot.\par \par \uc2 DAWN JACKSON-BLATNER (NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 The second part here is move your body. Your body needs to know that it is awake time. So I actually love jumping rope. I think it's so fun, and just even a couple of minutes, or stretch. I think that doesn't have to be much but just hello, good morning all body cells. and it'll get you going.\par \par \uc2 DAWN JACKSON-BLATNER (NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 And then come on, man, we need to have a balanced colorful breakfast. So if you are somebody who is like a savory eater, maybe that's avocado toast with eggs and spinach or if you're a sweet eater maybe it's my - I love this. This is, like, peanut butter and jelly style oatmeal where you have a bowl of oatmeal with some nut butter and mashed berries. But those three things are powerhouses to get your day started right.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Okay, so the thing that I have a problem with is about 3:00 in the afternoon, I'm like totally flat, right? So what can you snack on in the afternoon when you're starting to lose steam?\par \par \uc2 DAWN JACKSON-BLATNER (NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 Okay, here's the dynamic duo for a snack. It's produce and protein. And those two things come together to get you full, keep you full, but most importantly balance your blood sugar so that you have steady sustained energy through the afternoon. So that could be like an apple and a handful of nuts, something simple but it's really powerful. I also love to make DIY energy drinks. This would be something like a macha latte which has less caffeine than coffee, but still a little jolt, or a DIY electrolyte drink or a low sugar green juice.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Good tips, Dawn. Thanks so much for being with us this morning.\par \par \uc2 DAWN JACKSON-BLATNER (NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 Oh, well, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Rob, now, over to you.\par \par \uc2 ROB MARCIANO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Makes me wanna slice up an apple, dip it in some peanut butter. That's my go-to in the afternoon. Love it. All right. I love this. Not this picture but what I'm about to show you, which is the before and after. This is the Lake Charles, Louisiana next rad dopler radar which got ripped apart during hurricane Laura five months ago with 140-mile-an-hour winds. They were ahead of schedule and managed to fix it and just put on the new (inaudible) which, I think, weighs about 8,000 pounds. It is operational, protecting the lives of the residents there in Southwest Louisiana.\par \par \uc2 ROB MARCIANO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Some snow, we're watching this, from Des Moines to Chicago to Detroit, even New York down to D.C. over the next several days. Could see several inches. Time now for a look at your local forecast.\par \par \uc2 ROB MARCIANO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Truth be told, we're still working through the Halloween chocolate which doesn't go too badly over the peanut butter on that apple in the afternoon for a snack. Dan, over to you.\par \par \uc2 DAN HARRIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) I appreciate the confession, Rob. You wear it well. We'll see you in the next half hour.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020210129eh1n00060\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORK FROM HOME TAX? WORKERS MAY FACE DOUBLE TAX CHARGE THIS YEAR\b0\par\par\uc2 426 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 January 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 COVID-19, DEATHS, VARIANT, PINSKY, JACKSON, BAHL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEATH EVERY 30 SECONDS\par \par \uc2 VACCINE, ROLLOUT, CUOMO, MURPHY, FAUCI, KABSY, COLLINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROLLOUT SLOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 IMPEACHMENT, TRUMP, MILLER, SIEGE, CAPITOL, ROSEN, CLARK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEEP FREEZE\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, NAVALNY, PROTESTS, RIOT POLICE, POISONED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KREMLIN CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 MEGA MILLIONS, JACKPOT, WINNER, NOVI, MICHIGAN\par \par \uc2 KING, DEATH, COVID-19, "LARRY KING LIVE", INTERVIEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CELEBRATING A LEGEND\par \par \uc2 TAXES, WORK-FROM-HOME, SETBACK, CRANEY, WALZCAK, GREEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORK FROM HOME TAX?\par \par \uc2 TOM LLAMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Back now with "Your Money." Millions of Americans working from home could face another setback this tax season. Here's ABC's Deirdre Bolton.\par \par \uc2 DEIRDRE BOLTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, for many working remotely because of COVID, a potentially nasty surprise coming at tax time. Tax bills not just from one state, but two.\par \par \uc2 PAUL CRANEY (SPOKESMAN MASSACHUSETTS FISCAL ALLIANCE)\par \par \uc2 I would argue it's, it's really bad economics, and it's cruel.\par \par \uc2 DEIRDRE BOLTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Among those who may get hit, employees working from home for companies headquartered in a different state. In general, states demand income tax based on where the work gets done. That's why professional athletes pay income taxes in all states where they play games. But several states demand tax from workers employed outside their borders because they are home to the employing companies. Now, with so many Americans working remotely, double tax bills may hit hundreds of thousands.\par \par \uc2 JARED WALZCAK (VICE PRESIDENT OF STATE PROJECTS AT THE TAX FOUNDATION)\par \par \uc2 The problem is, your home state, in many cases, will not offer you a credit for the work you did in another state, because from their perspective, you didn't leave their state.\par \par \uc2 DEIRDRE BOLTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Massachusetts adopted the same practice last spring. Employers like Rick Green be locations in five states worry.\par \par \uc2 RICK GREEN (OWNER 1A AUTO)\par \par \uc2 They could've done something that they, they had a relative who was sick or something and they, they, you know, they did it for all the right reasons, and then bang, they just get hit kind of out of nowhere.\par \par \uc2 DEIRDRE BOLTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Most states are facing budget shortfalls due to the slowing economy, which may inspire others to try to impose similar tax rules. Tom?\par \par \uc2 TOM LLAMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Deirdre, thank you.\par \par \uc2 TOM LLAMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) When we come back, how the \uc2 NFL\uc2  is thanking thousands of health-care workers during the biggest game of the year. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020210126eh1n00009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW THIS MORNING: WHERE TO FIND WORK NOW/WHERE THE JOBS ARE NOW THE HOTTEST SECTORS FOR JOB OPPORTUNITIES/HOW TO FIND AND GET NEW CAREER OPPORTUNITIES\b0\par\par\uc2 758 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 January 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, MCCARTHY, PELOSI, NEWHOUSE, SMITH, NORCROSS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, IMPEACHMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP IMPEACHED FOR SECOND TIME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSIDE THE WHITE HOUSE AFTER HISTORIC VOTE\par \par \uc2 IMPEACHMENT, HEARING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP IMPEACHED FOR A SECOND TIME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT FACES SENATE TRIAL AFTER HISTORIC HOUSE VOTE\par \par \uc2 SECURITY, CONTEE, BOWSER, TERROR PLOT, MEREDITH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATION ON ALERT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUTHORITIES WARN OF "WEEK OF SIEGE" BEING PLANNED BY EXTREMIST GROUPS\par \par \uc2 COVID, VACCINE, BARTLETT, DE BLASIO, PERSICHILLI, JONES\par \par \uc2 LOTTERY, MEGA MILLIONS, POWERBALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NO WINNER IN POWERBALL DRAWING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JACKPOTS SOARS TO $640 MILLION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 BLAKE, SHOOTING, CRUMP, SHESKEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JACOB BLAKE SPEAKS OUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST INTERVIEW SINCE POLICE SHOOTING THAT SPARKED NATIONWIDE PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, FINANCES, DE BLASIO, RICHERSON, CONTRACTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP'S FINANCIAL FALLOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW YORK CITY CANCELS CONTRACTS WITH PRESIDENT'S COMPANY\par \par \uc2 HARDEN, \uc2 BROOKLYN NETS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IMPEACHED AGAIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING OVERNIGHT\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT TRUMP/IMPEACHED TWICE/FIRST TIME IN US HISTORY/SENATE TRIAL/HISTORIC HOUSE VOTE/CONDEMNATION/"POLITICAL VIOLENCE"\par \par \uc2 VACCINATIONS/"MEGA-SITES"/SUPPLIES RUNNING LOW/JOHNSON AND JOHNSON PHASE 3 TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CORONAVIRUS EMERGENCY - THE LATEST\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY CENTER HONOREES/LIFETIME ACHIEVEMENT/MARIAH CAREY/VOICE/TEXAS CONFUSING STREET SIGNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KENNEDY CENTER ANNOUNCES 2021 HONOREES\par \par \uc2 BACKSTREET BOY/NICK CARTER/LAUREN CARTER/EXPECTING AFTER MISCARRIAGES/5 MONTHS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: @LAURENKITTCARTER/INSTAGRAM, @NICKCARTER/INSTAGRAM\par \par \uc2 JOB SEEKERS/OPPORTUNITIES/HOTTEST SECTORS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) We're going to turn now to the millions of Americans facing financial hardships through the pandemic, some encouraging news for job seekers this morning. There are so many opportunities out there, it helps if you know where to look. Rebecca Jarvis is back, has some answers for us. Good morning, again, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yes, nice to see you again, Robin. And that is the good news, there are some job openings out there. You do have to know where to look and you also have to know how to tell your story in this environment.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNEMPLOYMENT\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, while a new year brings a fresh start, many are still feeling the economic effects of the pandemic with more than 19 million Americans still filing unemployment claims each week, but for job seekers, there's a bright spot.\par \par \uc2 KARIN KIMBROUGH (CHIEF ECONOMIST\par \par \uc2 Despite having a really tough situation right now in the labor market, we do see opportunities.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 LINKEDIN\uc2  LOGO\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2  currently has more than 14 million job listings available right now. The top five roles most in demand, salesperson, registered nurse, software engineer, JavaScript developer, and food delivery driver. And for those looking to make their own schedule, companies like Taskrabbit and \uc2 Instacart\uc2  are continuously hiring with \uc2 Instacart\uc2  also increasing its corporate roles by 50 percent in the first six months of the year.\par \par \uc2 KARIN KIMBROUGH (CHIEF ECONOMIST\par \par \uc2 A lot of people don't realize that they actually have quite transferable skills. If you're already adept in working in say a restaurant you can use that experience that you've had face-to-face with people and transfer that as a customer service specialist.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Remember, those fundamental skills, strong communication, attention to detail, resourcefulness, problem solver, Robin, these are the kind of skills that no manager wants to turn down. They are in need no matter what the job is.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) All right, so, Rebecca, let's say you want to go for one of these jobs, but it's not in a field that you were in prior to the pandemic. What's your advice?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHERE ARE THE JOBS: FREE ONLINE TRAINING\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Well, my advice is to look at all of the free courses that are online right now. They are free and they will help you build those technical skills. The EdX courses, there's tutorials by \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 . A number of companies are even offering, like \uc2 Google\uc2  for example and \uc2 IBM\uc2 , certificates so that you don't even need a college degree in order to get jobs in some of these tech companies that are hiring right now because of the explosion of e-commerce and the pandemic, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Such great suggestions. Thanks so much, Rebecca. And now Ginger. How'd you celebrate your birthday, Ginger?\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020210120eh1e0000j\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Date\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/2021 to 06/10/2026\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalp